WEBVTT

00:00:01.076 --> 00:00:09.567
An embed puts your agent on another website, for visitors who are not signed in. Here is how one is made, and what a visitor can and cannot do.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:22.806
In the web app, open Embeds and press New embed. A panel opens beside the list. Give it a name, a title and a welcome message. The preview is the real widget, and it follows every change you make.

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:34.656
Tick only the tools a visitor may use. Everything unticked is off. Then list the websites that may show the chat. A wildcard is refused, and at least one website is required.

00:00:35.157 --> 00:00:46.101
Save it, and the panel stays open as the edit of your embed, with the snippet to paste: plain HTML, an iframe, a web component, or curl. Copy puts it on your clipboard.

00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:54.946
On the docs site, the chat bubble appears. A visitor asks a question, and the answer streams in, using only the tool the embed lists.

00:00:55.447 --> 00:01:05.346
Back in the web app, open the embed from the list. The counters show what happened, as real numbers. Rotate the key to end every open session, then close the panel.

00:01:05.848 --> 00:01:21.485
The page is the list of your embeds. Search by name or website, and filter by on, off or expired. The switch turns an embed off at once, and visitors are answered as if it never existed. Delete removes one for good, and asks first.

00:01:21.991 --> 00:01:28.135
That is an anonymous docs agent. The tool list, the limits and the allowed websites are what protect it.
